⍝ Divide.tc
⍝ ═════════

⍝@ test4.

      ⎕IO←1

      ⍝ Precond: A numeric, B numeric and non-zero
      ⍝ inv: A÷B ←→ A×÷B   (divide = multiply by the reciprocal)
      A ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      B ← ⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0)
      B ← B+(B=0)                    ⍝ avoid division by zero
      ∧/(A÷B) = A×÷B
1

      ⍝ inv: A ←→ B×(A÷B)   (division is the inverse of multiplication)
      ⍝ uses tolerant = rather than exact ≡, since A÷B is in general not
      ⍝ exactly representable as a double when B does not divide A
      ∧/(B×(A÷B)) = A
1

      ⍝ Precond: B non-zero and A an exact multiple of B, so A÷B stays
      ⍝ an exact int (no rounding to worry about)
      ⍝ inv: A ←→ B×(A÷B)   (exact this time - checked with ≡)
      B ← 1+99∣|⎕RVAL 0
      K ← 1+9999∣|(⎕RVAL 1 (,5) (,0 1 0 0 0))
      A ← B×K
      A ≡ B×(A÷B)
1

      ⍝ Precond: Big is at the int64 boundary and evenly divisible by
      ⍝ 7, so Big÷7 stays an exact int (Quad_CR reports type 16), but
      ⍝ multiplying it back by 7 crosses the conservative LARGE_INT
      ⍝ threshold and is promoted to float by ×
      ⍝ (IntCell::bif_multiply_ii()) - yet the result still matches Big
      ⍝ exactly
      ⍝ inv: Big ←→ 7×(Big÷7)
      Big ← 9223372036854775807
      Big ≡ 7×(Big÷7)
1
